# meraki/schema — Australian English
#
# A variation on en, not a copy of it. Every key absent here is inherited, so this file holds only
# what Australia says differently: four words out of a hundred and ten entries.
#
# The chain comes from the file name. Asking for `en-AU` loads `en.mfr` and lays this over it, key
# by key. Nothing here declares a parent, because a file that named its own would be free to
# disagree with what it is called.
#
# Note what is *not* here. `postalCodeFormat` reads "That is not a valid {$part} for the country
# you chose", and because {$part} is resolved through the part.* entries below, redefining
# `part.postal_code` fixes every message that mentions one. A variant that stays this short is a
# variant working properly.
#
# Note also what does not belong here. This is the language a reader speaks, not the country an
# address is in — an Australian reader can be entering a New Zealand address — so nothing here may
# assume that {$bound} is Australia.

@locale = en_AU

part.postal_code = postcode
part.subdivision = state
part.locality = suburb
part.dependent_locality = locality
